 Why this is better
 Using pkg-config here is more portable because liblldpctl-dev provides the package metadata and include/library paths, instead of you assuming a soname or install path. Debian package metadata shows lldpctl.pc is installed by liblldpctl-dev. (packages.debian.org)

 One small note
 If your environment does not define an imported target for PkgConfig::LLDPCTL for some reason, use the classic variables instead:

 CMake
 target_include_directories(lldp-observer PUBLIC ${LLDPCTL_INCLUDE_DIRS})
 target_link_libraries(lldp-observer PRIVATE ${LLDPCTL_LIBRARIES})
 target_link_directories(lldp-observer PRIVATE ${LLDPCTL_LIBRARY_DIRS})
 target_compile_options(lldp-observer PRIVATE ${LLDPCTL_CFLAGS_OTHER})
 But IMPORTED_TARGET is the cleaner modern form.

